From 5f5b5b7df107f0c5a84612a8273f1b195b02dbda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OE-Alliance <oe-alliance@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 23:59:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] v3d nxpl: place the GLES GUI above the DVB video plane

The Broadcom DVB decoder and the NXPL native window both default to z-order
zero.  On the V3D/NXPL MIPS implementation this leaves their relative order
undefined and the opaque parts of Kodi's EGL surface can hide decoded video.

Use the established NXPL GUI z-order of one.  The DVB video plane remains at
zero, while the EGL alpha channel still lets video show through Kodi's
transparent fullscreen background and keeps OSD/subtitles above it.
---
 xbmc/windowing/egl/EGLNativeTypeV3DNXPL.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/egl/EGLNativeTypeV3DNXPL.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/egl/EGLNativeTypeV3DNXPL.cpp
index 67857b033d..f622e2c76a 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/egl/EGLNativeTypeV3DNXPL.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/egl/EGLNativeTypeV3DNXPL.cpp
@@ -178,7 +178,7 @@ bool CEGLNativeTypeV3D::CreateNativeWindow()
   nativeWindow.height = 720;
   nativeWindow.stretch = false;
   nativeWindow.clientID = 0;
-  nativeWindow.zOrder = 0;
+  nativeWindow.zOrder = 1;
 
   m_nativeWindow = NXPL_CreateNativeWindowEXT(&nativeWindow);
   if (!m_nativeWindow)
